    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (one acceptance test class) passes with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate detection feature for `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` while carrying a different `telephone`, it's still created and flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\nChanges made, following the existing \"captured-at-creation\" pattern used by fields like `bulkSignupWarning`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). The build regenerates `OwnerDto` from this spec.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` persisted fields with `@Column` mappings and getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them by name (no mapper change needed).\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate BOOLEAN` and `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)` to the create pipeline (after the hard-duplicate `identityKey` check has already passed). It scans existing owners for one sharing the last name and a present, exact postcode with a differing telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate` true with `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id (lowest id when several match), or false/null otherwise. It runs before persistence so it only considers pre-existing owners.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` test and the full suite pass.",
